<h2 class="wp-block-wd-title title wd-ab9a01b2">FAQs</h2>
<!-- /wp:wd/title -->

<!-- wp:wd/accordion {"blockId":"230cbdac-fa0f-47f4-8a47-58a2a9de4dfb","blockVersion":"2","allClosed":true,"openerSize":"14","titleTpFontFamily":"var(\u002d\u002dwd-title-font)","titleTpFontSize":"28","titleTpFontSizeTablet":"22","titleTpFontSizeMobile":"20","marginBottomTablet":"0"} -->
<div class="wp-block-wd-accordion wd-accordion wd-style-default wd-titles-start wd-opener-style-arrow wd-opener-pos-end wd-230cbdac" data-state="all"><!-- wp:wd/accordion-pane {"blockId":"e5a4569a-2490-406e-b39d-287355e5d0e6","blockVersion":"2","borderColorVariable":"\u002d\u002dwd-primary-color","borderWidthTop":"2"} -->
<div class="wp-block-wd-accordion-pane wd-accordion-item wd-e5a4569a"><div class="wd-accordion-title wd-role-btn" tabindex="0"><div class="wd-accordion-title-text"><span>My order hasn't arrived yet. Where is it?</span></div><span class="wd-accordion-opener"></span></div><div class="wd-accordion-content"><div class="wd-accordion-content-inner"><!-- wp:wd/paragraph {"blockId":"61764eb3-9066-4dd7-8079-e12647be645d","blockVersion":"2"} -->
<p class="wp-block-wd-paragraph wd-61764eb3">A client that’s unhappy for a reason is a problem, a client that’s unhappy though he or her can’t quite put a finger on it is worse. Chances are there wasn’t collaboration, communication, and checkpoints, there wasn’t a process agreed upon or specified with the granularity required.</p>
<!-- /wp:wd/paragraph -->

<!-- wp:wd/paragraph {"blockId":"e84cec68-57d8-4186-baf3-f57d6a464d0a","blockVersion":"2"} -->
<p class="wp-block-wd-paragraph wd-e84cec68">It’s content strategy gone awry right from the start. Forswearing the use of Lorem Ipsum wouldn’t have helped, won’t help now. It’s like saying you’re a bad designer, use less bold text, don’t use italics in every other paragraph. True enough, but that’s not all that it takes to get things back on track.</p>
<!-- /wp:wd/paragraph --></div></div></div>
<!-- /wp:wd/accordion-pane -->

<!-- wp:wd/accordion-pane {"blockId":"154e703f-9952-4c47-be07-98b3a894d708","blockVersion":"2","borderType":"solid","borderColorCode":"#dfddd6","borderWidthTop":"1","borderWidthBottom":"1"} -->
<div class="wp-block-wd-accordion-pane wd-accordion-item wd-154e703f"><div class="wd-accordion-title wd-role-btn" tabindex="0"><div class="wd-accordion-title-text"><span>Do you deliver on public holidays?</span></div><span class="wd-accordion-opener"></span></div><div class="wd-accordion-content"><div class="wd-accordion-content-inner"><!-- wp:wd/paragraph {"blockId":"ad6c2849-a575-43c7-9f2c-c703af2f9ec8","blockVersion":"2"} -->
<p class="wp-block-wd-paragraph wd-ad6c2849">If that’s what you think how bout the other way around? How can you evaluate content without design? No typography, no colors, no layout, no styles, all those things that convey the important signals that go beyond the mere textual, hierarchies of information, weight, emphasis, oblique stresses, priorities, all those subtle cues that also have visual and emotional appeal to the reader. Rigid proponents of content strategy may shun the use of dummy copy but then designers might want to ask them to provide style sheets with the copy decks they supply that are in tune with the design direction they require.</p>
<!-- /wp:wd/paragraph --></div></div></div>
<!-- /wp:wd/accordion-pane -->

<!-- wp:wd/accordion-pane {"blockId":"98d126d9-7112-4d2d-8573-ca9e49559305","blockVersion":"2"} -->
<div class="wp-block-wd-accordion-pane wd-accordion-item wd-98d126d9"><div class="wd-accordion-title wd-role-btn" tabindex="0"><div class="wd-accordion-title-text"><span>Do you deliver to my postcode?</span></div><span class="wd-accordion-opener"></span></div><div class="wd-accordion-content"><div class="wd-accordion-content-inner"><!-- wp:wd/paragraph {"blockId":"b50ced29-e52b-4f2a-81e7-6c632c2efc41","blockVersion":"2"} -->
<p class="wp-block-wd-paragraph wd-b50ced29">A client that’s unhappy for a reason is a problem, a client that’s unhappy though he or her can’t quite put a finger on it is worse. Chances are there wasn’t collaboration, communication, and checkpoints, there wasn’t a process agreed upon or specified with the granularity required.</p>
<!-- /wp:wd/paragraph -->

<!-- wp:wd/paragraph {"blockId":"d754c621-a439-4e9c-a1d4-19b2b68d15df","blockVersion":"2"} -->
<p class="wp-block-wd-paragraph wd-d754c621">It’s content strategy gone awry right from the start. Forswearing the use of Lorem Ipsum wouldn’t have helped, won’t help now. It’s like saying you’re a bad designer, use less bold text, don’t use italics in every other paragraph. True enough, but that’s not all that it takes to get things back on track.</p>
<!-- /wp:wd/paragraph --></div></div></div>
<!-- /wp:wd/accordion-pane -->

<!-- wp:wd/accordion-pane {"blockId":"b75876f2-7f7b-40a9-9580-ae271f4b46ec","blockVersion":"2"} -->
<div class="wp-block-wd-accordion-pane wd-accordion-item wd-b75876f2"><div class="wd-accordion-title wd-role-btn" tabindex="0"><div class="wd-accordion-title-text"><span>Is next-day delivery available on all orders?</span></div><span class="wd-accordion-opener"></span></div><div class="wd-accordion-content"><div class="wd-accordion-content-inner"><!-- wp:wd/paragraph {"blockId":"50b87d6b-eb0d-4eb3-96a9-f83dcbdab518","blockVersion":"2"} -->
