<!-- /wp:wd/paragraph --></div></div></div>
<!-- /wp:wd/accordion-pane -->

<!-- wp:wd/accordion-pane {"blockId":"0b402f9a-9442-413b-bad1-12368c5a42db","blockVersion":"2","marginBottom":"-40","borderType":"none"} -->
<div class="wp-block-wd-accordion-pane wd-accordion-item wd-0b402f9a"><div class="wd-accordion-title wd-role-btn" tabindex="0"><div class="wd-accordion-title-text"><span>Do I need to be there to sign for delivery?</span></div><span class="wd-accordion-opener"></span></div><div class="wd-accordion-content"><div class="wd-accordion-content-inner"><!-- wp:wd/paragraph {"blockId":"ad6c2849-a575-43c7-9f2c-c703af2f9ec8","blockVersion":"2"} -->
<p class="wp-block-wd-paragraph wd-ad6c2849">A client that’s unhappy for a reason is a problem, a client that’s unhappy though he or her can’t quite put a finger on it is worse. Chances are there wasn’t collaboration, communication, and checkpoints, there wasn’t a process agreed upon or specified with the granularity required.</p>
